jection takes the share of the month that days 1 to 23 delivered in Jun, Jul and Aug (74%, 73%, 71%) and applies it to 420, giving about 577. Straight line run rate gives 548. Week 1 brought 145 onboardings, week 2 brought 107, week 3 brought 118, and 22 to 23 Sep brought 50. Aug reached 327 by this point and closed at 462, but Aug had a 31 Aug deadline that pulled its last week forward; Sept has no deadline, so read the projection as a ceiling and the straight line as a floor. 552 sits between the two, needing about 19 a day for the last seven days against a run rate of 18. 600 needs about 26 a day.","daily":"7-day average line. Week 1 signups 243, week 2 161, week 3 205. 22 Sep was the best day of the campaign at 60 signups from 46 referrers; 23 Sep held up at 36 signups from 35 referrers. No single referrer sent more than 25 signups in the last day, so nothing to flag. Today is not charted until the day is complete.","ladder":"276 onboarded referees belong to people who have not unlocked anything yet. At the usual 70 to 75% activation rate that is roughly 200 more Polaroids in the pipeline. Exporter 133487 has unlocked Ray-Ban at 6 and has not claimed, so is going for the iPhone. Exporter 224027 has reached AirPods at 3 and has not claimed. Four people are one activation from AirPods. 77 people have unlocked at least the Polaroid and 20 have claimed it, every claim at exactly one activation.","cohorts":"The lift on the activated base is +22% for the month to date, rate 1.59% against 1.30% in Aug. Past referrers (1b, +56%) and recently dormant users (1.2, +35%) carry it. Never-referrers (1a) are at 1.07% against 1.05%, essentially level with Aug: the campaign has reached about as many first-time referrers as last month, not more.","mix":"63% of campaign referrers have never referred before, but first-timers are only level with Aug on a like-for-like basis; the referrer increase is mostly repeats. Past power referrers (3+ prior) bring 2.68 signups each and only 43% onboard, so they are sharing wider and shallower.","weeklyQuality":"Across all referrals (38679 excluded) Sept 1-day onboarding is running in the low 40s, below the 52 to 56% of Mar to Aug. The gap sits with referrers sending 2 or more signups: single-signup senders convert to a next-day onboarding at 54%, people sending 2 or more at 36%. The 21 Sep week is still filling in.","claims":"20 of the 77 people who unlocked a reward have claimed it, all at the Polaroid rung and all at exactly one activation. The two referrers at AirPods and above, exporter 224027 at three and exporter 133487 at six, have not claimed, which is the behaviour the ladder was designed for.","popupHeader":"Mixpanel, Sept 1 to 23. Every event so far is at the first rung.","popup":["Still nobody has pressed keep referring. Eighteen confirmed the camera claim, and six opened the claim without confirming. At the first rung the trade is a camera already earned against two more activations at 17 to 19 days each, and for most people that is a bad bet.","One referrer who has not claimed kept referring anyway and is now at AirPods, so the zero on keep referring measures button presses rather than intent. Worth checking with Tech whether that button changes any state."],"referrers":["489 people have referred on the campaign, excluding the flagged referrer 85276. 403 of them (82%) sent exactly one signup, and those convert to onboarding at 63%. The other 86 sent 338 signups between them, 46% of the total, but only 147 onboarded (44%) and 33 activated. Volume and ladder progress are not the same thing: the top ten senders produced 130 signups, 44 onboardings and 13 activations, and exporter 38154's 35 signups have yielded 6 onboardings and 1 activation.","The healthiest cohort is repeat referrers with 1 to 2 prior achievements. 88 people, 1.6 signups each, 59% onboarding, 25 activations. They go a little deeper than first-timers without the dilution. Past power referrers (3+ achieved) send 2.7 each but only 43% onboard. First-timers are the largest group at 307 (63%) and convert normally at 54%.","171 referrers (35%) have zero onboarded referees against 214 signups. That is the cheapest recovery pool in the campaign: the referrer already made the ask, the referee already signed up, someone just needs to finish the form.","89 referrers (18%) have never activated on Skydo themselves. They brought 132 signups, 64 onboarded, 6 activated. 30 onboarded in September and referred within days. The ladder is being promoted by people who have not used the product, which explains some of the weaker referee quality.","Referrers who signed up in the past but never achieved a milestone (60 of them) brought 72 signups, 41 onboarded and 6 activated, in line with first-timers.","77 have unlocked at least the Polaroid. 20 have claimed it. The 57 who have not are still on the ladder, including the one referrer at AirPods and the one at Ray-Ban."],"refereeQuality":["Referees from single-signup referrers look about as good as August's and a little better on value. 54% onboard in a day against 55%, 19% activate within 10 days against 16%, and the median first settlement is about $2,155 against $1,867.","Referees from 2+ signup referrers are a different population. 36% onboard in a day and 44% in a week, against 65% in August. Their median first settlement is about $272, roughly a seventh of the norm. The few who activate do so quickly (21% within 10 days), but the stream is mostly noise: 312 signups, 81 old enough to judge. The flagged referrer's signups are left out and would have made this worse.","The mix has moved toward freelancers, 58% of Sept onboardings against 49% in Aug, with companies down from 12% to 10%. The company referees Sept does bring are activating better than August's, 15% within 10 days against 8%, though that is 20 people.","Stated monthly volume is unchanged where it matters. Referees stating $10K or more are 4.5% of Aug onboardings and 4.9% of Sept. More Sept referees fill in the field at all (62% against 54%), and nearly all of the extra answers are under $10K. None of the Sept $10K+ referees has activated yet, which is worth watching since these are the ones Sales would chase.","Net: the campaign is not lowering the quality of a referral from a normal referrer. It is adding a second stream of low-intent signups from people chasing the higher rungs, and that stream should be judged separately rather than averaged in."],"qualityHeader":"Referees deduped to their first referral, 38679 and internal ids excluded. Aug vs Sept 1 to 23, flagged referrer 85276 excluded. Money in USD at the Sept median rate of Rs 95 per dollar.","qualityWindow":"Activation is measured on a 10-day window because the campaign is 23 days old and the usual 17 to 19 day median means most campaign referees have not had time to activate yet. Read the last two columns as early signal, not a result.","excluded":"Excluded from every campaign number on this page: exporter 85276 (freelancer, onboarded May 2025, never transacted). 120 signups, 119 of them between 02:47 and 09:54 IST on 24 Sep, one every 56 seconds on median. 115 distinct phone numbers, so these look like real people, but 83 never picked a business type and 2 have onboarded. The pattern fits a link posted into a large group rather than personal referrals. Left in, it would push signups to 833, signups per referrer to 1.74 and first-timer onboarding to 43%. Onboardings are barely affected. Worth an Ops review before any of these referees activate."}}